---
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "How long does Spamhaus delisting take?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Approved SBL and XBL removals typically apply within the hour. Repeat listings after unresolved compromises re-lock quickly." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Why does my IP keep getting relisted?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Persistent listings mean the underlying source is still sending: an open relay, a compromised account, or a misconfigured newsletter stack. Delisting without fixing the source loops forever." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "What is the difference between SBL and XBL?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "SBL lists spam sources and Spamhaus observes them actively; XBL lists exploited machines found through botnet tracking. The fixes differ: content and behavior for SBL, malware cleanup for XBL." } }
  ],
};
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

---
<BaseLayout title="How to Get Off the Spamhaus Blocklist (SBL, XBL, PBL)"  description="Spamhaus delisting guide: identify which Spamhaus list you are on, fix the root cause, and request removal the right way."  
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["Email Authentication", "/email-authentication/"], ["Email Deliverability", "/email-deliverability/"], ["Spamhaus Removal"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-deliverability/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Deliverability</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Spamhaus Removal</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Get Off the Spamhaus Blocklist</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      Spamhaus operates several lists with different meanings and different cures. Half of all
      delisting pain comes from treating them as one thing. Identify yours first, fix the cause,
      then request removal.
    </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Spamhaus lists</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>List</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">SBL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Close the spam source</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">XBL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Clean the compromise</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">PBL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Policy removal</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">DBL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Fix the domain</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60">
      <table class="pdns-table">
        <thead><tr><th>List</th><th>Why you are on it</th><th>The fix</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">SBL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Spam operations, phishing, malware associated with your IP or domain.</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Remove the malicious content/compromise, then contact Spamhaus with evidence.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">XBL / CSS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Your IP shows exploit or open-proxy behavior.</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Clean the server, close the proxy, request re-scan.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">PBL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Your IP is in dynamic/residential space that should not send direct mail.</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Send through your ISP's smarthost or a provider; or use the PBL removal form if genuinely static.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">DBL (domain)</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Your domain appeared in spam payloads.</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Stop the campaign/compromise sending it, then request DBL removal.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="rich-text mt-10">
      <h2>The procedure</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Look up your IP or domain</strong> in the Spamhaus lookup (zen.spamhaus.org returns codes telling you which list fired). Our <a href="/blacklist-checker/">blacklist checker</a> gives an honest first pass, with the caveat that Spamhaus refuses public-resolver queries.</li>
        <li><strong>Fix the root cause completely.</strong> Compromised account, open redirect, misconfigured server, abused form: the listing returns if you only request removal.</li>
        <li><strong>Request removal</strong> through the Spamhaus form for your list. Free for small volumes; include what happened and what changed.</li>
        <li><strong>Watch propagation.</strong> Delisting flows to users of the data within hours; some filters cache longer.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Preventing the encore</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Authenticate (SPF, DKIM, <a href="/dmarc/">DMARC</a>) so compromise is visible in reports, not discovered via listings.</li>
        <li>Monitor: re-run the <a href="/blacklist-checker/">blacklist checker</a> weekly, or let <a href="/pricing/">monitoring</a> do it.</li>
      </ul>
      
<h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does Spamhaus delisting take?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Approved SBL and XBL removals typically apply within the hour. Repeat listings after unresolved compromises re-lock quickly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why does my IP keep getting relisted?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Persistent listings mean the underlying source is still sending: an open relay, a compromised account, or a misconfigured newsletter stack. Delisting without fixing the source loops forever.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is the difference between SBL and XBL?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">SBL lists spam sources and Spamhaus observes them actively; XBL lists exploited machines found through botnet tracking. The fixes differ: content and behavior for SBL, malware cleanup for XBL.</p></details></div>
      <h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/get-off-barracuda-blocklist/">Barracuda delisting</a> and <a href="/sorbs-delisting-guide/">SORBS delisting</a></li>
        <li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/">Why emails go to spam</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
